in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @nl

# @mirror/lens — mirror's observation/projection family.
#
# The recognition (2026-06-06, Reed + Alex → Mara): the substrate already
# has four transports onto one runtime (λsh / CLI / MCP / LSP, per
# docs/specs/the-convergence.md §1.2) and two measurement-shape grammars
# (@lens/transit and @mirror/refract). All six are LENSES at mirror's
# altitude — different shapes through which the substrate is observed,
# rendered back to the consumer, or measured against a hardware floor.
# Family naming closes the recognition.
#
# === Discipline ===
#
# A lens IS:
#
#   - an observation surface: same five-operation algebra, different
#     input/output language. The runtime evaluates the same algebra;
#     each lens renders it for a different audience (terminal, agent,
#     editor, interactive shell, runtime cost, grammar-graph spectrum).
#   - a projection: the lens does not OWN state. State lives in the
#     daemon; the lens reads through to the same graph through the
#     same algebra. Two lenses pointed at the same node MUST see the
#     same eigenvalue (per the-convergence.md §1.4); divergence is a
#     bug by construction.
#   - composable: lens reports compose under the existing
#     `Transparency<P>` monoid (per fragmentation/docs/specs/lens-transit.md
#     §3). No parallel combine; the algebra is borrowed verbatim.
#
# === Species under this family ===
#
# Transport lenses (the four-transport convergence per
# docs/specs/the-convergence.md §1):
#
#   @mirror/lens/cli      terminal lens. Porcelain commands over argv +
#                          flags; eigenboard-tagged exit codes. The
#                          human-in-CI lens. Migrated from
#                          shards/mirror/cli.mirror 2026-06-06 (Mara).
#   @mirror/lens/shell    interactive lens. The λsh transport per
#                          docs/specs/lambda-shell.md. mq expressions
#                          with eigenboard-tagged prompt; the
#                          human-at-terminal lens.
#   @mirror/lens/mcp      agent lens. stdio JSON-RPC tool dispatch.
#                          Tool args parse to mq; output is mirror-text
#                          in content[]. The agent-Claude lens.
#   @mirror/lens/lsp      editor lens. tower-lsp adapter; LSP methods
#                          on ranges map to mq expressions scoped to
#                          document nodes. The editor lens.
#
# Measurement-shape lenses:
#
#   @mirror/lens/transit  runtime-cost lens. Lifts Taut's
#                          fragmentation/docs/specs/lens-transit.md to
#                          mirror's altitude. Six properties (WallClock,
#                          FpPrecision, CachePressure, Allocation,
#                          BranchMisses, BudgetConsumption) bounded
#                          per platform by hardware floors. Carries
#                          verdicts as `Transparency<P>` over substrate
#                          paths. The cost-of-passage lens.
#   @mirror/lens/refract  grammar-graph spectrum lens. Reads the five
#                          Void dualities (entropy / spectral / cheeger /
#                          ricci / mixing) over the grammar graph and
#                          surfaces them as verdicts. Per
#                          docs/specs/trace-kintsugi-pipeline.md;
#                          "refract IS bench wearing its real name."
#                          The shape-of-the-grammar lens.
#
# === Why one family ===
#
# Transports and measurements are not separate kinds. Both project the
# same algebra through a typed surface; both compose under the same
# Transparency<P> monoid; both observe state without owning it. The
# convergence spec already named the four transports "adapters onto the
# same five operations"; lens-transit declared its shape as a sibling
# Transparency consumer; refract was already calling itself "bench at
# the grammar-graph altitude." The family unifies the recognition.
#
# The substrate-pull cost of NOT naming this: every new measurement or
# transport lands at an ad-hoc altitude (`@cli`, `@lsp`, `@bench`,
# `@trace`) and the cross-cutting discipline (Transparency-as-carrier,
# eigenboard-tagged-output, daemon-as-regulator) has to be re-justified
# per surface. With the family, the discipline IS the family.
#
# Note on `refract` as namespace: the operation-altitude rename closed
# 2026-06-04 (refract → settle) was at the algebra altitude; lens
# absorbs the optical metaphor at the family altitude. `refract` stays
# as a NAMESPACE name for the grammar-graph spectrum lens (where the
# Void dualities disperse the grammar's structure into measurements);
# the operation `settle` is unchanged.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/the-convergence.md (four-transport recognition),
#               docs/specs/lambda-shell.md (λsh / shell transport),
#               docs/specs/cli-as-prism.md (cli surface; the-convergence
#               sibling),
#               docs/specs/trace-kintsugi-pipeline.md (refract as bench
#               at grammar-graph altitude),
#               fragmentation/docs/specs/lens-transit.md (transit's
#               Transparency<P> consumer shape),
#               docs/insights/2026-06-06-benchmarking-glass-sweep.md
#               (the recognition that lens-transit IS the benchmarking
#               glass).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]].
# Related shards: lens/cli.mirror (the terminal lens, the first
#                 migrated species),
#                 lens/shell.mirror, lens/mcp.mirror, lens/lsp.mirror
#                 (transport lens family headers),
#                 lens/transit.mirror, lens/refract.mirror (measurement
#                 lens family headers).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/mirror/lens.mirror`
# declares `@mirror/lens` and only that.

out @mirror/lens
